.\" acompat-test.1 -- userland/packages/acompat.  BSD-2-Clause, see acompat/LICENSE.
.TH ACOMPAT-TEST 1 "2026-10-30" "acompat 0.1" "Amix add-on commands"
.SH NAME
acompat\-test \- check libacompat (libamixcompat) on this machine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/local/bin/acompat\-test
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acompat\-test
is linked against the installed
.B libacompat.a
and calls every function it provides:
.BR snprintf ,
.BR vsnprintf ,
.BR setenv ,
.BR unsetenv ,
.BR strcasecmp ,
.BR strncasecmp ,
.BR mkstemp ,
.B usleep
and
.BR gettimeofday .
It proves the library on this machine's processor and C library, which a
test on the build host cannot.
.PP
It prints the library's version, then one
.B ok
or
.B FAIL
line per check, then a summary
.RI ( n " passed, " m " failed" ).
The floating-point check runs last and says so first: on a machine with no
68881 or 68882 any floating-point conversion in the stock C library dies with
SIGSYS, and the earlier results are already printed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every check passed, 1 otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acompat (3)
